evals.prompt:
Review this Mu Server upload handler and give a concrete patch plan without changing code yet:

```java
serverBuilder
    .withMaxRequestSize(Long.MAX_VALUE)
    .addHandler(Method.POST, "/upload", (request, response, params) -> {
        UploadedFile f = request.uploadedFile("file");
        executor.submit(() -> {
            if (f.contentType().startsWith("image/")) {
                f.saveTo(new File("public/uploads/" + f.filename()));
            }
        });
        response.write("queued");
    });
```

The service receives bursts of hundreds of browser multipart uploads and occasionally leaves corrupt or overwritten files. Explain the Mu-specific body, threading, temporary-file, and lifecycle behavior behind the failures; propose bounded storage, quota, validation, atomic publication, and cleanup semantics; and list focused black-box tests. We are on 2.4.1 today but expect to move to Mu Server 3. Preserve our existing build and do not add a library just to access uploads.
